# claim-hygiene.allowlist — site-level entries for LEGITIMATE affirmative
# statements that match the #163 §12 overclaim detector.
#
# Entry shape (exactly three fields, '|'-separated):
#     path-glob | source-line-substring | reason
# The exemption applies ONLY when BOTH the changed file path matches the glob
# AND the substring occurs in the ADDED line. Whole-file exemption is
# deliberately unsupported (same policy as assert-hygiene.allowlist):
# a new unregistered line in an already-allowlisted file still fails.
#
# Currently empty: the 2026-08-23 repository audit found zero violations,
# and all in-tree mentions of the phrase class are negations or
# mentioned-as-a-phrase (policy text), which the line-level negation and
# quote escapes already cover.
